# Package repositories pkg installs from (pkg update, pkg install NAME,
# pkg search, pkg upgrade). One a line:
#
#   NAME URL                  its INDEX must be signed with the key in
#                             /etc/pkg/keys/NAME.pub ("ed25519 HEX")
#   NAME URL key=PATH         ... with the key in PATH
#   NAME URL signature=none   unsigned (a local folder you trust)
#
# URL is http://, https:// (the server's certificate is checked against
# /etc/ssl/certs), file:///path or /path. A repository is a folder of
# packages with the INDEX that `scripts/ports.py repo FOLDER --key KEY`
# writes on the build machine (make ports-repo); make the key with
# `scripts/ports.py keygen SECRET PUBLIC` and copy PUBLIC here.
#
# Example:
# ports https://packages.example.org/freepascalos/x86_64
